### Ymmo Data/AI service — manual tests (VS Code REST Client)
### The service runs on port 8000. Make sure the DB is up and seeded.

@base = http://localhost:8000

### Health (expect database "up")
GET {{base}}/health

### Price trends — all cities (avg price per m² by city & category)
GET {{base}}/trends

### Price trends — filtered on one city
GET {{base}}/trends?city=Paris

### Popular properties (by view count)
GET {{base}}/popular

### Popular — top 5
GET {{base}}/popular?limit=5

### Strategic zones (opportunity score per city)
GET {{base}}/zones

### Head-office dashboard KPIs
GET {{base}}/dashboard/kpis

### Price estimate — apartment, Paris, 70 m²
POST {{base}}/estimate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "city": "Paris", "category_id": 2, "area": 70 }

### Price estimate — house, Aix-en-Provence, 120 m²
POST {{base}}/estimate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "city": "Aix-en-Provence", "category_id": 1, "area": 120 }

### Price estimate — city with no data (falls back, or 404 if DB is empty)
POST {{base}}/estimate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "city": "Bordeaux", "category_id": 2, "area": 80 }
